# Flutter Responsive UI Standards

All screens and new UI in `lib/` must work on **mobile (<600px)**, **tablet (600–1099px)**, and **desktop (≥1100px)**.

## Required imports

```dart
import 'package:helty/src/core/responsive.dart';
```

## Breakpoints — use AppBreakpoints only

```dart
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    final bp = AppBreakpoints.fromWidth(constraints.maxWidth);
    // ...
  },
)
```

Never use magic numbers (`width >= 800`, `SizedBox(width: 250)` on toolbars).

Thresholds: mobile `< 600`, tablet `600–1099`, desktop `≥ 1100`, max content `1280`.

## Page body pattern

Wrap page content in `ResponsiveBody`:

```dart
// Fill viewport — lists, split panels, Column + Expanded (default)
body: ResponsiveBody(
  builder: (context, bp) => Column(
    crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.stretch,
    children: [ /* content */ ],
  ),
),

// Scrollable forms / detail pages
body: ResponsiveBody(
  expand: false,
  builder: (context, bp) => SingleChildScrollView(
    child: /* form fields */,
  ),
),
```

## Flex layout rules

- Page bodies with `Column` + `Expanded` use `ResponsiveBody` (default `expand: true`)
- Scrollable forms use `ResponsiveBody(expand: false)` + `SingleChildScrollView`
- Panel widgets with internal `Expanded` (`SelectUser`, chat/help lists) must be wrapped in `Expanded` or `FlexPanel` — never as a non-flex sibling in a `Column`
- `ResponsiveRowColumn` inside scroll views: set `stackFill: false`
- Reusable flex panels: wrap with `FlexPanel` when embedding outside a bounded scaffold body

## Layout rules

| Pattern | Widget |
|---------|--------|
| Side-by-side panels | `ResponsiveRowColumn` |
| KPI / form grids | `ResponsiveWrapGrid` (1 / 2 / 3 cols) |
| Toolbar actions | `ResponsiveToolbar` or `Wrap` |
| DataTable / wide tables | `ResponsiveDataTable` |
| App shell with nav | `ResponsiveScaffold` (sidebar ≥1100) |

## Mobile requirements

- Stack multi-column `Row` layouts when `bp.isMobile`
- Search fields and inputs: full width (`Expanded`), not fixed `SizedBox(width: …)`
- Tables: horizontal scroll via `ResponsiveDataTable`, min width 720 on mobile
- Dialogs: `width: min(560, screenWidth - 32)`

## Deprecated — do not create new usages

- `AccountsBreakpoints`, `CmdBreakpoints`, `BillingBreakpoints` — use `AppBreakpoints`
- Inline `width >= 700/800/1100` checks — use `AppBreakpoints`

## Before merging

Verify no `RenderFlex overflow` at viewport widths: **360px**, **768px**, **1280px**.
